The build bootstrap materializes a modified copy of CodexBar 0.49.3 in
`CodexBar-upstream/`, based on upstream tag `v0.49.3` at commit
`fc57a317cee4a8f84962c62c45e4502085f6fc79`. CodexBar is copyright (c) 2026
Peter Steinberger and is distributed under the MIT License. The bootstrap
fetches its original repository and license before applying the reviewable
patches under `patches/codexbar/`.
The second patch adds an optional isolated cost-cache path and a parser test;
it does not change the default cache or account credential handling.

The third patch exports canonical per-source reports from CodexBar's existing
fork reconciliation, calendar grouping, read-time pricing and optional Pi/OMP
report builders. It does not change the token parser or default cost command.
The daily-history interface adapts `CostHistoryChartMenuView.swift` behavior.
The planner adds independent retention and explicit account attribution; it no
longer maintains a separate JavaScript pricing table. API-equivalent values
are estimates from local usage and a public price catalog, not billed charges.

